@page "/docs/accessibility/component-status"
@inject Registry Registry
@inject ApiMetadata Api

@* Every component with what has been checked on it, in three columns that mean different things: its keys (the API
   metadata's Keyboard table), the automated audit of its docs pages (site/IzzyBlazor.Site/.izzy/audit-baseline.json: remake
   the numbers in Run when the baseline is remade), and screen readers (artifacts/a11y-audit/SCREEN-READER-PASS.md: add a
   component to ScreenReaders as the pass reaches it). A cell says what was done, never "conforms". After Syncfusion's
   per-component table (Nov 25, 2026), which has no column for what wasn't tested. *@

<ArticlePage Section="accessibility" Slug="component-status">
    <Lead>
        This page lists every component with what has been checked on it and how. A check by a tool and a test
        by a person are separate columns, since
        <Anchor Href="docs/accessibility/automated-and-manual">they answer different questions</Anchor>. Where a
        test hasn't been done, the cell says so.
    </Lead>
    <ChildContent>
        <Heading Level="2">What the columns mean</Heading>
        <Table Items="Meanings" Caption="The columns of the status table" Size="ControlSize.Sm" Class="site-params" Bordered="false">
            <Columns>
                <TemplateColumn Title="Column" Width="Length.Rem(10)">@context!.Name</TemplateColumn>
                <TemplateColumn Title="Says">@context!.Text</TemplateColumn>
            </Columns>
        </Table>

        <Heading Level="2">The automated audit</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            <Anchor Href="docs/accessibility/audit">izzy audit</Anchor> ran over this site on @Run.On:
            @Run.Pages pages, each at 1440 and 375 pixels wide, in light and dark, and once in forced colors.
            It runs axe-core and <Anchor Href="docs/accessibility/audit-checks">four checks of its own</Anchor>
            on every example of every component. The run had @Run.Findings findings. None was real and none
            needed a person: @Run.FalsePositives were false positives of a rule, @Run.DemoPages came from a docs
            page showing a component several times, and @Run.Accepted are accepted with a reason, on docs
            examples that show a color on purpose.
        </TextBlock>
        <TextBlock>
            So the Audit column is the same for every component today. It says that the rules found nothing on
            the component's examples as they load. It doesn't cover a closed dialog or menu, the order of the
            keyboard or what a screen reader says.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Screen readers</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            A pass with screen readers has started and isn't done. Names, roles and states are checked in the
            browser's accessibility tree, which is what a screen reader reads, but that is not the same as
            listening to one. The pass covers VoiceOver with Safari, then NVDA with Chrome and Firefox, JAWS and
            Narrator on Windows, and VoiceOver and TalkBack on phones. A component's cell names the screen
            readers it has been through. If one gets something wrong,
            <Anchor Href="https://github.com/IzzyBlazor/izzyblazor/issues" External>report it as an issue</Anchor>.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Known gaps</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            A component with a known gap is marked in the table. The
            <Anchor Href="docs/accessibility/overview#known-gaps">overview</Anchor> describes each gap and its
            workaround. One gap is shared by every field and switch: their borders have about 2:1 contrast
            against the page.
        </TextBlock>

        @foreach (var category in Registry.Categories)
        {
            <Heading Level="2">@category</Heading>
            <Table Items="@Rows(category)" Caption="@($"{category}: accessibility status")" Size="ControlSize.Sm" Class="site-params site-params-prose site-params-status" Bordered="false">
                <Columns>
                    <TemplateColumn Title="Component"><Anchor Href="@context!.Href">@context.Name</Anchor></TemplateColumn>
                    <TemplateColumn Title="Keys">
                        @if (context!.Keys)
                        {
                            <Anchor Href="@($"{context.Href}#keyboard-navigation")">Listed</Anchor>
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <text>The browser's own</text>
                        }
                    </TemplateColumn>
                    <TemplateColumn Title="Audit">@(context!.Gap ? "No findings; one known gap" : "No findings")</TemplateColumn>
                    <TemplateColumn Title="Screen readers">@context!.ScreenReaders</TemplateColumn>
                </Columns>
            </Table>
        }
    </ChildContent>
</ArticlePage>

@code {
    private sealed record Row(string Name, string Text);

    private sealed record Status(string Name, string Href, bool Keys, bool Gap, string ScreenReaders);

    // The run the Audit column reports: .izzy/audit-baseline.json, remade Nov 25, 2026 after the triage.
    private static readonly (string On, string Pages, int Findings, int FalsePositives, int DemoPages, int Accepted) Run =
        ("November 25, 2026", "543", 88, 27, 58, 3);

    // Components the screen reader pass has reached, with what was run. Everything else is "Not yet".
    private static readonly Dictionary<string, string> ScreenReaders = new()
    {
        ["Switch"] = "VoiceOver with Safari: read through",
        ["LiveRegion"] = "VoiceOver with Safari: started",
    };

    // Components with a gap in the overview's Known gaps.
    private static readonly HashSet<string> Gaps = ["NumberField"];

    private static readonly Row[] Meanings =
    [
        new("Keys", "\"Listed\" links the component's Keyboard navigation table, for keys that IzzyBlazor's script adds. \"The browser's own\" means the component is a native element or takes no keys, and has no keys of its own to list."),
        new("Audit", "What izzy audit found on the component's docs pages, in every example, as they load."),
        new("Screen readers", "The screen readers a person has run the component's examples through, or \"Not yet\"."),
    ];

    private List<Status> Rows(string category) =>
        [.. Registry.InCategory(category).Select(c => new Status(
            c.DisplayName, Registry.OverviewHref(c), Api.Component(c.Name)?.Keyboard is { Count: > 0 }, Gaps.Contains(c.Name),
            ScreenReaders.GetValueOrDefault(c.Name, "Not yet")))];
}
